.TH LANGUAGETOOL-PORTAL 1 "October 2026" "scripts" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
languagetool-portal \- self-service token portal for LanguageTool with Authentik forward auth
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B languagetool-portal
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
[\fB\-H\fR|\fB\-\-host\fR \fIHOST\fR]
[\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-port\fR \fIPORT\fR]
[\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-users-file\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-u\fR|\fB\-\-server-url\fR \fIURL\fR]
[\fB\-\-in-place\fR]
[\fB\-\-setup-service\fR]
[\fB\-\-remove-service\fR]
[\fB\-\-status\fR]
[\fB\-\-print-service\fR]
[\fB\-\-user\fR|\fB\-\-system\fR]
[\fB\-\-run-as\fR \fIUSER\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBlanguagetool-portal\fR is a lightweight, zero-dependency autonomous HTTP service for managing and rotating personal LanguageTool API tokens. It is built strictly on the Python 3 standard library.
.PP
The portal is designed to operate behind a reverse proxy (such as HAProxy) configured with Authentik Forward Auth. Authentik validates user sessions and passes the authenticated identity in the \fBX-authentik-username\fR header.
.PP
Key features:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAutomated Onboarding:\fR When an authenticated user accesses the portal for the first time, a cryptographically secure 32-character hexadecimal token (\fBsecrets.token_hex(16)\fR) is generated and stored in \fBusers.txt\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBIdempotence & Rotation:\fR Reloading the portal displays the current token without regenerating. Clicking "Сгенерировать новый ключ" invalidates the previous token and generates a new one.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAtomic & In-Place Writes:\fR Safely updates \fBusers.txt\fR using temporary files and \fBos.replace\fR or direct in-place modification protected by \fBfcntl.flock\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSanitization:\fR Rigorously validates usernames to prevent file format injection (colons, newlines, control characters).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBOk/Healthcheck:\fR Provides \fBGET /healthz\fR returning \fB200 OK\fR for HAProxy health checks without authentication.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSelf-Contained Dark UI:\fR Modern Dracula/GitHub Dark themed UI with no external CDN or web dependencies (fonts/icons are fully embedded). Includes one-click copy buttons and Obsidian setup instructions.
.SH DOCKER & PODMAN INODE CAVEAT
LanguageTool re-reads \fBusers.txt\fR on the fly by monitoring the file's modification time (\fBlastModified\fR).
.PP
When deploying LanguageTool in containers (e.g. via Podman Quadlet or Docker), avoid mounting the single file directly:
.PP
.nf
  # AVOID: Linux bind-mount attaches to a specific host inode
  Volume=%h/stacks/languagetool/data/users.txt:/LanguageTool/users.txt:ro,Z
.fi
.PP
With atomic \fBos.replace\fR, a new host inode is allocated, causing container bind mounts of single files to become disconnected from updates.
.PP
.B Recommended Solution:
Mount the parent directory instead:
.PP
.nf
  Volume=%h/stacks/languagetool/data:/LanguageTool/data:ro,Z
.fi
.PP
And configure LanguageTool's \fBconfig.properties\fR:
.PP
.nf
  passwortLoginAccessListPath=/LanguageTool/data/users.txt
.fi
.PP
If you must mount a single file, run \fBlanguagetool-portal\fR with \fB\-\-in-place\fR (or \fBLT_IN_PLACE=true\fR) so the script overwrites the file without altering its inode.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Displays usage information and exits.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-host " \fIHOST\fR"
Listening network interface (default: \fB127.0.0.1\fR).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " \fIPORT\fR"
Listening port (default: \fB8012\fR).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-users-file " \fIPATH\fR"
Path to LanguageTool user credentials file (default: \fB~/stacks/languagetool/data/users.txt\fR).
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-server-url " \fIURL\fR"
Public LanguageTool API endpoint shown in the portal UI (default: \fBhttps://lt.nada.mu/v2\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-in-place
Modifies \fBusers.txt\fR in-place using \fBfcntl.flock\fR, keeping the file inode unchanged for container single-file mounts.
.TP
.BR \-\-db-url " \fIURL\fR"
PostgreSQL connection URI (e.g. \fBpostgresql://user:pass@host:5432/dbname\fR). Enables Mode B (server-side dictionaries sync into the \fBusers\fR table).
.TP
.BR \-\-db-host " \fIHOST\fR"
PostgreSQL server hostname.
.TP
.BR \-\-db-port " \fIPORT\fR"
PostgreSQL server port (default: \fB5432\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-db-name " \fIDBNAME\fR"
PostgreSQL database name.
.TP
.BR \-\-db-user " \fIUSER\fR"
PostgreSQL username.
.TP
.BR \-\-db-password " \fIPASS\fR"
PostgreSQL password.
.TP
.B \-\-setup-service
Installs, enables, and starts the systemd service (\fBlanguagetool-portal.service\fR) with pre-flight initialization of \fBusers.txt\fR (permissions 0664). Defaults to user service if unprivileged, or system service if root.
.TP
.B \-\-remove-service
Stops, disables, and deletes the systemd service.
.TP
.B \-\-status
Performs an HTTP healthcheck against the portal, checks \fBusers.txt\fR stats and permissions (0664), tests PostgreSQL connection (if enabled), and inspects systemd service state.
.TP
.B \-\-print-service
Prints the systemd unit file content to stdout and exits.
.TP
.B \-\-user
Forces installation/removal of user-level systemd service (\fB~/.config/systemd/user\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-system
Forces installation/removal of system-level service (\fB/etc/systemd/system\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-run-as " \fIUSER\fR"
Specifies the system user account for the systemd unit when installing system-wide (default: \fBapps\fR).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Displays program version and exits.
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B LT_PORTAL_HOST
Listening interface (default: \fB127.0.0.1\fR).
.TP
.B LT_PORTAL_PORT
Listening port (default: \fB8012\fR).
.TP
.B LT_USERS_FILE
Path to \fBusers.txt\fR (default: \fB~/stacks/languagetool/data/users.txt\fR).
.TP
.B LT_SERVER_URL
Public LanguageTool endpoint (default: \fBhttps://lt.nada.mu/v2\fR).
.TP
.B LT_IN_PLACE
Enable in-place writing when set to \fBtrue\fR or \fB1\fR.
.TP
.B LT_DB_URL ", " DATABASE_URL
PostgreSQL connection string for stateful dictionary synchronization.
.TP
.B PGHOST ", " PGPORT ", " PGDATABASE ", " PGUSER ", " PGPASSWORD
Standard PostgreSQL client environment variables.
.SH ENDPOINTS
.TP
.B GET /
Renders portal UI for authenticated user from \fBX-authentik-username\fR. Returns 401 if header is absent.
.TP
.B POST /
Regenerates user API token and issues a 303 See Other redirect to \fBGET /\fR.
.TP
.B GET /healthz
Monitoring healthcheck. Returns \fB200 OK\fR (\fBOK\en\fR). No authentication required.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run portal interactively on default loopback port 8012:
.PP
.nf
  languagetool-portal
.fi
.PP
Run as user \fBapps\fR with custom file path:
.PP
.nf
  languagetool-portal --users-file /home/apps/stacks/languagetool/data/users.txt
.fi
.PP
Install and start as a systemd user service:
.PP
.nf
  languagetool-portal --setup-service
.fi
.PP
Check health and service status:
.PP
.nf
  languagetool-portal --status
.fi
